<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-SFE wheat futures edge up in slow trade.</title>
<headline>RTRS-SFE wheat futures edge up in slow trade.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Sydney Futures Exchange wheat market remained quiet on Monday with six lots of the nearby March contract trading.</p>
<p>March 1997 rose by A$3.00 to A$180.00 on the trade.</p>
<p>The market was quiet with little interest, Phil Lindsay of Ord Minnett Jardine Fleming Futures Ltd said.</p>
<p>The Australian Wheat Board's recent agreement6 to supply 900,000 tonnes of wheat to Japan was helping the local market to firm. It appeared likely that the firming trend would continue, he said.  </p>
